Decision: keep the recovery sentence in English for the model-facing tool protocol, persist its structured tool_interrupted metadata, and replace it with localized user-facing text when Beaver renders saved tool details.

Reason: recovered tool results are visible after session reload. The model needs one stable protocol payload, while users must see a clear message in their selected language. Structured metadata is the authority that connects those two representations; matching human prose would be fragile.

The message is provided in all seven supported languages. The UI explains that the outcome is unknown and asks the user to verify external state before retrying. The unrelated non-null assertion on optional context progress was also removed.

Validation: 16 interrupted-tail tests, saved-history and error-localization tests, TypeScript, and the full frontend lint pass.
